    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$3.89 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) including the cheese and the tortillas. Compare that to what a birria taco truck charges for three tacos and a small cup of consomme.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eChipotles in adobo replace a bag of dried chiles.\u003c/strong\u003e One or two small cans deliver smoke, heat and color with no toasting or soaking. That is a shortcut worth taking on a weeknight.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCheese is the second biggest line here, so buy it on sale and freeze it.\u003c/strong\u003e Shredded blends freeze and thaw without losing anything, and this recipe uses a lot of it.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCorn tortillas are cheaper than flour and they crisp better.\u003c/strong\u003e Dipping them in the consomme and griddling them is the whole move, and corn holds up to it.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eDo not throw out the braising liquid.\u003c/strong\u003e That consomme is free flavor you already paid for. Portion it into small containers and reheat it alongside."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cube the pork shoulder, season it with salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, ground cumin and dried oregano, and sear it hard in the vegetable oil in batches.",
                    "Add the seared pork to the slow cooker with the diced onion, minced garlic, the chipotles in adobo, the chicken broth and the bay leaves.",
                    "Cook on low for 8 hours, until the pork falls apart when you press it with a spoon.",
                    "Lift the meat out and shred it, then skim the red fat off the top of the braising liquid and save that fat separately. Keep the rest of the liquid as your consomme.",
                    "Dip each tortilla in the reserved red fat, lay it on a hot griddle, add shredded pork and the Mexican cheese blend, fold it over, and crisp both sides.",
                    "Stir the lime juice into the consomme, chop the cilantro to scatter over everything, and spoon the salsa over the tacos at the end."
                ],
